{"run_id": "7ca9b2904c634a9494d71c56ad7c3458", "stage": "tool_result", "at": 1791023641.2579007, "tool": "read_project_context", "arguments": {"path": "README.md", "line": 33, "context_lines": 30}, "status": "ok", "error_code": null, "result": {"path": "README.md", "start_line": 3, "end_line": 63, "lines": [{"line": 3, "text": "**Requests** is a simple, yet elegant, HTTP library."}, {"line": 4, "text": ""}, {"line": 5, "text": "```python"}, {"line": 6, "text": ">>> import requests"}, {"line": 7, "text": ">>> r = requests.get('https://httpbin.org/basic-auth/user/pass', auth=('user', 'pass'))"}, {"line": 8, "text": ">>> r.status_code"}, {"line": 9, "text": "200"}, {"line": 10, "text": ">>> r.headers['content-type']"}, {"line": 11, "text": "'application/json; charset=utf8'"}, {"line": 12, "text": ">>> r.encoding"}, {"line": 13, "text": "'utf-8'"}, {"line": 14, "text": ">>> r.text"}, {"line": 15, "text": "'{\"authenticated\": true, ...'"}, {"line": 16, "text": ">>> r.json()"}, {"line": 17, "text": "{'authenticated': True, ...}"}, {"line": 18, "text": "```"}, {"line": 19, "text": ""}, {"line": 20, "text": "Requests allows you to send HTTP/1.1 requests extremely easily. There’s no need to manually add query strings to your URLs, or to form-encode your `PUT` & `POST` data — but nowadays, just use the `json` method!"}, {"line": 21, "text": ""}, {"line": 22, "text": "Requests is one of the most downloaded Python packages today, pulling in around `30M downloads / week`— according to GitHub, Requests is currently [depended upon](https://github.com/psf/requests/network/dependents?package_id=UGFja2FnZS01NzA4OTExNg%3D%3D) by `1,000,000+` repositories. You may certain"}, {"line": 23, "text": ""}, {"line": 24, "text": "[![Downloads](https://static.pepy.tech/badge/requests/month)](https://pepy.tech/project/requests)"}, {"line": 25, "text": "[![Supported Versions](https://img.shields.io/pypi/pyversions/requests.svg)](https://pypi.org/project/requests)"}, {"line": 26, "text": "[![Contributors](https://img.shields.io/github/contributors/psf/requests.svg)](https://github.com/psf/requests/graphs/contributors)"}, {"line": 27, "text": ""}, {"line": 28, "text": "## Installing Requests and Supported Versions"}, {"line": 29, "text": ""}, {"line": 30, "text": "Requests is available on PyPI:"}, {"line": 31, "text": ""}, {"line": 32, "text": "```console"}, {"line": 33, "text": "$ python -m pip install requests"}, {"line": 34, "text": "```"}, {"line": 35, "text": ""}, {"line": 36, "text": "Requests officially supports Python 3.9+."}, {"line": 37, "text": ""}, {"line": 38, "text": "## Supported Features & Best–Practices"}, {"line": 39, "text": ""}, {"line": 40, "text": "Requests is ready for the demands of building robust and reliable HTTP–speaking applications, for the needs of today."}, {"line": 41, "text": ""}, {"line": 42, "text": "- Keep-Alive & Connection Pooling"}, {"line": 43, "text": "- International Domains and URLs"}, {"line": 44, "text": "- Sessions with Cookie Persistence"}, {"line": 45, "text": "- Browser-style TLS/SSL Verification"}, {"line": 46, "text": "- Basic & Digest Authentication"}, {"line": 47, "text": "- Familiar `dict`–like Cookies"}, {"line": 48, "text": "- Automatic Content Decompression and Decoding"}, {"line": 49, "text": "- Multi-part File Uploads"}, {"line": 50, "text": "- SOCKS Proxy Support"}, {"line": 51, "text": "- Connection Timeouts"}, {"line": 52, "text": "- Streaming Downloads"}, {"line": 53, "text": "- Automatic honoring of `.netrc`"}, {"line": 54, "text": "- Chunked HTTP Requests"}, {"line": 55, "text": ""}, {"line": 56, "text": "## API Reference and User Guide available on [Read the Docs](https://requests.readthedocs.io)"}, {"line": 57, "text": ""}, {"line": 58, "text": "[![Read the Docs](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/psf/requests/main/ext/ss.png)](https://requests.readthedocs.io)"}, {"line": 59, "text": ""}, {"line": 60, "text": "## Cloning the repository"}, {"line": 61, "text": ""}, {"line": 62, "text": "When cloning the Requests repository, you may need to add the `-c"}, {"line": 63, "text": "fetch.fsck.badTimezone=ignore` flag to avoid an error about a bad commit timestamp (see"}]}}
